According to an ancient book labeled "gazateer" she had reached the
lair of Medusa.  Well equipped with a pair of jumping boots, Serra said
"Let's go!" On the way, another one of those creepy demons tried
(unsuccessfully) to get inside her armour.

After finishing off Medusa, Serra decided to head up to the mines (she
needed some candles).  On the way up, she stopped at a barbecue pit and
made many offerings.  In return for her devotion, she was given the
rustrpoof Snikersnee.

Serra had never really liked one-handed weapons, but forced herself to
practice with Snikersnee (just in case something happened to her
tsurugi).  She disliked gaijin weapons even more than one-handed
weapons and so Excalibur stayed in her bag for the duration.

Somewhere along the way, a mindflayer showed up.  A bit of scribbling
with a magic marker and she knew she wouldn't be running into any more
of them. Upon reaching Minetown, she bought a scroll of genocide and
blessed it, just so that she could get rid of rust monsters and
disenchanters.

After wandering around for a bit, she was finally experienced enough to
do the quest (t=3D24725).

