After getting the Tsurugi of Muramasa, Serra relocated her 25ish
spellbooks to a single chest on the eleventh level (well protected by
some nice fireworks graffiti, of course) ... carrying the library of
alexandria around was getting to be a bit burdensome, and that's a
very_bad_thing(tm).

She then had this nice big barbecue (emptying her three /oCreateMonster
and draining her energy several times) before praying and getting
crowned.

Continuing downwards, she reached a gaijin castle.  This was one giant
cluster, even with conflict!  Serra didn't have any means of opening
the drawbridge, so she had to destroy it with a spell.  A nice scroll
of earth provided her with the means of bridging the moat.

After clearing out the throne room, she rested on another throne, and
felt "much, much better", summoned an audience, and genocide green
slimes.

She also went swimming to blank a bunch of scrolls and create a bunch
of bottled water.  When all was said and done, one potion of holy water
became 39 potions of holy water and 43 blessed scrolls of blank paper.

The wand of wishing was (0:3), and she got a nice spellbook of remove
curse, this obnoxiously gaudy fireproof shirt, and 5 sharpies.

Serra went on rather enjoyable poetry writing festival.  ToM,
Snikersnee, and Excalibur were all +7 now and all her armour is either
+4 or +5.  Her stack of 105 arrows was +1.  Scanned the level with
telepathy and saw a black dragon, so she genocided all dragons.

For the run through Gehennom, Serra had 39 potions of holy water, 20
blessed scrolls of remove curse, and the remove curse spell (at
skilled).  Overkill, perhaps, but you can *NEVER* have too may ways of
removing curses in hell.

