Serra continued the run downwards, and stopped writing very detailed
notes in the blessed notebook of gVim.  On reaching the Vally of the
Dead she had two questions:  "Why is there a peaceful dwarf lord
wandering about?" and "Can I buy some more protection?"

Asmodeus was just an annoyance (he didn't cause a single point of
damage) to be chased off the upstair before being sliced and diced.

Juiblex tried to eat Serra and left her feeling rather ill (a
/oDigging, a unicorn horn, and a slice by ToM took care of him).

On the 37th level, a nurse kept bothering Serra.  Seeing how this was
Gehennom, she felt it would be unwise to disrobe and submit to a
medical examination:  "The razor-sharp blade cuts the nurse in half!
You kill the nurse!"

Baalzebub was a bit of a challenge, because he stunned Serra with his
gaze a couple times before she could get her lenses off and her
blindfold on.  Once he was dislodged from the upstair, "whit!, whit!,
thud."

By this time, Serra was starting to forget spells (T ~=3D 44,000), and
her Bag of Holding was essentially full, so she went topside again,
bought some more protection from the Priestess of Moloch, took a bunch
of useless crap from her stash in the castle and her bag, zapped it
with her wands of polymorph, and got a whole bunch of useless crap for
her trouble.  She then relocated the library of Alexandria from the
eleventh level to the well-protected chest in the Castle.

After reading up, she went to go visit Vlad, got the "oLifeSaving and
yet another wish from his throne (blessed /oDeath, as she didn't have
one yet).

A short while later, and "Mr. Orcus, I really appreicate you wasting
all those /oDeath charges, no really I do!"

On the way down to mark the vibrating square, Serra saw that the Wizard
was surrounded by a whole-flock-o-gremlins.  (She also dug nice paths
between the stairs)  Seeing how this was night-time, she blessed
genocided 'g' as soon as possible.  After that, she marked this wierd
Vibrating Square with some lightning graffiti and a fortune cookie.

Now, Serra thought about what to do next ... See the Wizard or prepare
some more.  Caution persevered over bloodlust, so she went topside
again.  Serra reached the valley @ T=3D66429 and estimated the climb time
at 2,000 turns, not counting random level teleports with the AoY and
various Wizard "issues".  Then, she bought some more protection from
the Priestess of Moloch before killing her.  Lost her telepathy (you
murderer!) but she had an amulet for that.  Then she went and gave the
$58,000 up to the priest of Amaterasu Omikami a few levels up (Naked AC
=3D=3D -1).

Back at the Castle, with study time over (T=3D68733), now we're off to
see the Wizard, the wonderful Wizard of Yendor!

A bit later (T=3D70513), "Hi there Mr. Wizard" ZAP! "Damn that didn't
work?" ZAP! "Screw it!" SLICE!  And then the mysterious voice of
narration boomed those 17 words that every samurai just loves to hear:

"The razor-sharp blade cuts the Wizard of Yendor in half!"
"You kill the Wizard of Yendor!"

Serra took the Book of the Dead and made her way down to the Vibrating
Square.  She made some wierd light, alerted the audience with a very
special bell, and then read the Book of the Dead.  Dropped the book,
bell, and candelabrum.  Just then the Wizard decided to put in an
appearance, and, ok, so that's how you want to play it.  "Would you
care to step downstairs?"

Immediately the Wizard teleported to the altar room while Serra fought
her way to the courtyard.  Without liches and dragons (and with fire
resistance this time) it wasn't so bad.  Especially since the Wizard
was nice and distracted.

