Plane of Earth:  Yet Another Wizard, yet another Bisection.

Plane of Air:  Serra had a close call here.  She was engulfed and
pummelled by three air elementals in quick succession (HOW RUDE!).  She
was down to 4 HP when a steam vortex engulfed her.  After casting a
healing spell, she realized that the vortex wasn't hurting her, so she
decided to use vorticies for nice, irregularly scheduled time-outs
whenever one happened to come her way.

Plane of Fire:  Serra took advantage of the same vortex-induced
time-outs here, even though she didn't really need to (better safe than
sorry, especially when you're trying to ascend without any (extra/full)
healing potions and just the basic "healing" spell.)

Plane of Water:  Locating the portal took Serra far too long, then she
stupidly stepped on the portal before she should have.

Astral Plane:  Serra realised that she needed to eat before she went
charging the temple gates (especially since famine was in the center,
where she planned on going first).  After a quick snack of lichen, she
changed clothing.  Unfortunately, she was being hassled and forgot to
get her jumping boots out and put them on, so the girl who loved
footwear walked about bootless (she also forgot to put the bag of
holding back inside the oilskin sack).  Somewhere along the way, her
rings of slow digestion and free action were disintegrated.  Took care
of famine with the trusty /oDeath (0:8) that she was saving for the
Astral Plane.  Charged temple, and in keeping with the good fortune
Serra had been receiving so far, found the High Altar of Amaterasu
Omikami!

